{"id":"report-period-en-week-47","capability":"report_period_en","what":"2026-W47 周报：高原地震与洪水两条主题","match":{"includes":["2026-W47"]},"reply":{"headline":"A seismic week on the plateau","overview":"The week's material is dominated by one earthquake and one slow-onset flood. The Tibet earthquake supplied the only rapid measurements of the period: two agency magnitudes, a depth, and a sequence of aftershocks that grew with each advisory. The Yangtze flood moved more slowly, with gauge readings revised twice and a transfer count that changed between reports. Neither event produced a single authoritative number, and the edition keeps both readings where they differ. A third thread, satellite data releases, is filed under technology rather than hazards because nothing in those items describes a ground event.","themes":[{"heading":"Plateau tectonics","summary":"The Mw 7.1 Tibet earthquake and its aftershocks are covered through two agency readings, a depth of 12 km, and highway inspections near the epicenter. Where the agencies differ by 0.1 in magnitude, both figures are printed."},{"heading":"Flood risk","summary":"The middle Yangtze flood is documented through gauge levels that were revised twice and a transfer count that changed between reports. The edition states which gauge each level belongs to instead of averaging them."}]},"author":"英文主编（GEOHOT 英文腿，2026-11-23 核过中文版与条目原文）"}
{"id":"report-period-en-month-11","capability":"report_period_en","what":"2026-11 月报：三条主题","match":{"includes":["2026-11"]},"reply":{"headline":"November: measurements under revision","overview":"November's coverage turns on the difference between a first measurement and a settled one. Earthquake magnitudes were revised by tenths, flood levels by centimetres, and dataset versions by processing baseline. The month's theme is therefore not a single event but a habit: the edition states each figure with its source and its date, and declines to compress two readings into an average. Readers who need one number will find the agency's own, not ours.","themes":[{"heading":"Seismic monitoring","summary":"Two large earthquakes were reported during the month, each with more than one agency reading. The edition keeps the readings separate and notes the aftershock sequence."},{"heading":"Hydrology","summary":"Flood and drought conditions were reported from gauges and reservoirs, with several stages revised during the month."},{"heading":"Earth observation","summary":"Sentinel-2 and Landsat processing baselines changed during the month; the edition lists the version identifiers without restating measurement values."}]},"author":"英文主编（GEOHOT 英文腿，2026-11-23 核过中文版与条目原文）"}